    <p>
      More figures (git startup ~14 ms, one-shot execution 26.3 ms and other niubash-family numbers)
      on the <a href="/en/benchmarks/">benchmarks page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Release feed</h2>
    <p class="src-line">
      Latest 3 versions (changelogs.json, fetched 2026-10-19; the full feed lives on the
      <a href="/en/changelog/">changelog</a>):
    </p>
    <ul class="changelog-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Unreleased (release line, no date stamped)</strong>
        <span>
          WSL interop paths: <code>/mnt/X/…</code> operands fold in the same shape as <code>/X/…</code>
          and <code>X:\…</code> (#1172, byte-aligned with rubash's
          <code>windows_mnt_drive_argument</code>); latest release tag is v1.1.15 (repo-meta.json,
          measured 2026-10-19; Releases ship x64/ARM64 setup.exe plus a portable zip).
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>v1.1.14 (2026-10-17)</strong>
        <span>
          wpm: <code>links verify</code> reports per-path links not pointing at the current
          winuxcmd.exe; the <code>winuxcmd-shim.exe</code> mini-forwarder cuts shim dispatch from
          24.5 ms to 12.1 ms; <code>wpm update winuxcmd</code> no longer silently leaves command
          links on the old image; self-update rollback copies keep the newest two, auto-pruned.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>v1.1.13 (2026-10-17)</strong>
        <span>
          wpm: files held by running processes upgrade via rename-aside — either complete or
          untouched; forced-upgrade verified on a real install with 28 <code>fsmonitor--daemon</code>
          payload holders; <code>wpm clean staging/all</code> also clears parked
          <code>.wpm-old-&lt;pid&gt;</code> directories.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Related links</h2>
    <div class="link-cols">
      <div>
        <h3>On this site</h3>
        <ul>
